## 5. SAFETY PROTOCOLS

### License Validation
```python
ACCEPTED_LICENSES = ["MIT", "Apache-2.0", "BSD-3-Clause", "BSD-2-Clause", "ISC"]
REVIEW_LICENSES = ["LGPL-2.1", "LGPL-3.0"]
REJECTED_LICENSES = ["GPL-2.0", "GPL-3.0", "AGPL-3.0"]

def validate_license(license_text):
    if any(lic in license_text for lic in REJECTED_LICENSES):
        return "REJECT", "Viral license detected"
    elif any(lic in license_text for lic in REVIEW_LICENSES):
        return "REVIEW", "LGPL requires case-by-case review"
    elif any(lic in license_text for lic in ACCEPTED_LICENSES):
        return "ACCEPT", "License approved"
    else:
        return "UNKNOWN", "License not recognized"
```

### Security Scanning
```bash
# Run Trivy scan before integration
trivy fs --scanners vuln,secret,license _temp/[repo_name]

# Reject if:
# - Critical vulnerabilities found
# - Secrets detected
# - Incompatible license
```

### Isolation Testing
```python
# All assimilated tools must pass isolation tests
@pytest.mark.isolated
